To a large extent, faith follows the things heard from God’s Word. It is an aspect of the fruitage of God’s holy spirit.
Therefore, to demonstrate and exercise faith, we need holy spirit.
It would be a mistake to conclude that men and women of faith are born that way, that faith comes naturally.
The exemplary servants we read about in the Bible were people “with feelings like ours. ”
Although Moses ’ load seemed too heavy, he had, in fact, not been carrying it alone — neither would the 70 who were appointed to assist him carry it alone. Moses had been given holy spirit sufficient for the task.
