CAN YOU EXPLAIN?
In what sense does God yoke marriage mates together?
How can elders help Christians who have marital problems?
How should we view marriage?
WHEN Christians get married, they make a vow before God — a responsibility not to be taken lightly.
In the sense that he is the Originator of the marital arrangement, Jehovah has “yoked together ” those united in wedlock.
This yoke exists in God’s sight regardless of the laws that sanctioned the wedding.
Servants of Jehovah should view marriage as a binding arrangement whether they were his worshippers at the time of their wedding or not.
What questions will be considered in this article?
A successful marriage can result in great happiness. But what can be done if the marital bond is strained?
Can a weakened marriage be strengthened?
What help is there for those whose marital peace is threatened? WILL IT BE A JOY OR A HEARTACHE?
For instance, some youths begin dating when they are not ready for the responsibilities associated with married life.
If that is your experience, pray for God’s forgiveness and help. He does not remove the effects of a person’s past errors, but he does assist repentant ones to cope with trials.
Put your heart into pleasing him now and forever, and ‘ the joy of Jehovah will be your stronghold. ’ — Neh.
WHEN MARITAL BONDS ARE THREATENED
Regarding an unhappy marriage, what kind of thinking should be avoided?
Those who experience heartache in the marital relationship may wonder: ‘ Is my unhappy marriage really worth saving?
If only I could turn back the clock and begin again with another marriage mate! ’
Why not get a divorce?
If a Christian were to get a divorce, he or she may or may not be Scripturally free to get married again. Jesus said: “Whoever divorces his wife, except on the ground of fornication, and marries another commits adultery. ”
A failed marriage may cast doubt on one’s spiritual state. The apostle Paul raised this serious question: “If indeed any man does not know how to preside over his own household, how will he take care of God’s congregation? ”
In fact, when both mates profess to be Christians and yet their marriage fails, observers may think that such individuals do not really practice what they preach. — Rom.
What must be wrong if Christian mates decide to part?
When baptized marriage mates are planning to separate or to divorce each other on unscriptural grounds, something surely is spiritually wrong in their life.
If they were truly ‘ trusting in Jehovah with all their heart, ’ there would be little reason for believing that they could not avoid a failed marriage. — Read Proverbs 3: 5, 6.
How have some Christians been rewarded for their patient efforts in connection with marriage?
Consider what can happen in a religiously divided household.
Yes, because of his mate’s fine conduct, an unbeliever may embrace the true faith!
Such a saved marriage honors God and can be a great blessing for the husband, the wife, and any children they may have.
Or some time after the wedding, a spouse may become an inactive publisher.
THEY ARE READY TO ASSIST How will the elders view us if we seek their help?
Others have done so because of extreme physical abuse or the absolute endangerment of a Christian’s spirituality.
Whether to depart or not is a personal decision. However, the baptized mate ought to give this matter prayerful and honest consideration.
Under what circumstances could it be said that God has called married Christians to peace?
A Christian who is married to an unbeliever should earnestly endeavor to keep the marriage bond intact.
Yet, a Christian need not feel guilty if, despite the Christian’s sincere effort to preserve the union, an unbelieving mate refuses to remain with the believer.
Her marriage eventually ended in divorce, although she had put many years of effort into trying to save it.
I have a clear conscience.
What may happen if efforts are made to save a marriage? A Christian woman named Marilyn is glad that she trusted in God and put forth extra effort to save her marriage.
With respect to marriage, what should we be resolved to do?
And let us bear in mind that if we persevere in a divided household despite hardships, we may experience the joy of winning a mate over to true worship.
Christians who do not give up quickly on a strained marriage often enjoy a fine reward
