And there was no curse on the animals, including birds and fish; nor on the mountains, lakes, rivers, and seas; nor on the skies, clouds, sun, moon, and stars. Everywhere Abel looked, he saw evidence of the profound love, wisdom, and goodness of Jehovah God, the one who created all things.
Picture him tending his flock. A shepherd’s life required a great deal of walking.
No doubt he expressed many such thoughts in prayer, and his faith continued to grow as a result. In creation, Abel found a solid basis for faith in a loving Creator
Adam and Eve must have related to their sons the events in the garden of Eden that led to their expulsion.
