It would have to be something extremely significant to cause us to miss an opportunity to be united with our brothers in worship of Jehovah.
Many modern - day experiences give evidence that the angels are supporting our work and guiding us to those “rightly disposed for everlasting life. ” The earthly part of Jehovah’s organization is in place today and organized to support this all - important work.
Why should we make full use of the spiritual food we receive from Jehovah?
Jehovah has provided a bounteous supply of written spiritual food to give us strength. No doubt, you can think of a time when after reading a publication, you thought: ‘ That is exactly what I needed!
It is as if Jehovah had that written just for me! ’
Through these provisions, Jehovah does instruct and guide us.
He has said: “I shall make you have insight and instruct you in the way you should go. ” Do we strive to take in all the spiritual food we receive and meditate on it?
What can help us not to take our spiritual provisions for granted?
Printing branches ship literature to congregations near and far. Why is all this work done?
Who are supporting Jehovah’s arrangements in the heavens, and how can we show similar support on earth?
In the vision given to the apostle John, Jesus is seen riding on a white horse to conquer those rebelling against Jehovah.
How faith - strengthening it is to know that right behind Jesus are the faithful angels and with him are the anointed conquerors from the earth, who have already received their heavenly reward! What a superlative example that is of supporting Jehovah’s arrangements!
One way is by being in subjection to those taking the lead.
Additionally, do we discuss as a family how we can use our finances to support the worldwide work through our donations? Do we view as important the privilege of sharing in the upkeep of the Kingdom Hall?
Why must we constantly battle to live in harmony with Jehovah’s lofty purpose?
Finally, to endure and to stay in step with Jehovah’s organization, we must keep our personal lives consistent with the message that we bear by “making sure of what is acceptable to the Lord. ” Because of our imperfect flesh and the efforts of Satan and this wicked world, we are constantly battling negative influences in our lives.
Keeping the matter hidden will only make matters worse. Remember, David said that when he kept silent about his sins, ‘ his bones wore out through his groaning all day long. ’
Yes, hiding secret sins will just cause us to tire out emotionally and spiritually, but “he that is confessing and leaving them will be shown mercy. ” — Prov.
What should be our determination?
