LONDON, ENGLAND
Why do people need to hear the good news?
What do successful evangelizers do?
AN EVANGELIZER is someone who tells good news.
Immediately after the rebellion of our first parents, Jehovah announced the good news that the serpent — actually, Satan the Devil — will be destroyed.
Angels too are evangelizers. They themselves tell good news, and they assist others in spreading good news.
The apostle Paul urged his coworker Timothy: “Do the work of an evangelizer, fully accomplish your ministry. ” What is the good news that we as Jesus ’ followers spread?
It includes the reassuring truth that our heavenly Father, Jehovah, loves us. A key way that Jehovah God expresses his love is through his Kingdom.
They are taught that God is a mystery, that he is unknowable, or that he is cruel. For example, some religious leaders claim that God will punish bad people forever in a place of torment.
Questions open their mind and heart to accept the truth
Many who champion it declare that life came about without any intelligent direction.
Without doubt, the theory of evolution and false doctrines have contributed to the misery that mankind has experienced during the last days.
Instead, as the apostle Paul notes, they have left people “in darkness mentally, and alienated from the life that belongs to God. ”
In addition, the theory of evolution and false doctrines have hindered people from accepting the good news originating with God. — Read Ephesians 2: 11 - 13.
Questions also help them to reason so as to arrive at the correct conclusions
Even so, those who learn only from creation will not find answers to some of life’s most perplexing questions, such as these: Why does God allow suffering?
What is God’s purpose for the earth?
Does God care about me as an individual?
The only way that people can fully grasp the good news about God and his purpose is by studying the Bible. What a privilege we have to help people find answers to their questions!
To reach the heart of our listeners, though, we need to do more than inform them of facts; we must persuade them.
We can become more persuasive by following Jesus ’ example. Why was he so successful?
One reason is that he used questions effectively.
You might believe him. But what if he makes that promise even before he asks you any questions about your health?
No matter how talented the doctor may be, he needs to ask questions and listen to what your symptoms are before he can give any meaningful help. Similarly, if we are to help people accept the good news of the Kingdom, we must master the art of asking effective questions.
What may we be able to accomplish by imitating Jesus ’ way of teaching?
Jesus knew that well - chosen questions not only help a teacher learn about a student but also get the listener involved in the discussion. For example, when Jesus wanted to teach his disciples a lesson in humility, he first put a thought - provoking question to them.
To teach Peter how to reason on principles, Jesus asked him a multiple - choice question. On another occasion, when Jesus wanted to draw up what was in the heart of his disciples, he asked a series of viewpoint questions.
When we imitate Jesus by using questions effectively, we do at least three things. We discover how we can best help people, we overcome potential conversation stoppers, and we teach humble ones how they can benefit themselves.
How can you help a child to be more confident about sharing the good news?
Scenario 1: As a parent, what would you do if your teenage child expressed concern about being able to defend his belief in creation when talking with a classmate?
So rather than criticizing him or immediately offering advice, why not imitate Jesus ’ example and ask some viewpoint questions? How could you do so?
After reading with your child portions from the brochure The Origin of Life — Five Questions Worth Asking, you could ask what arguments he finds most thought provoking.
Let your child know that his reasons do not have to be exactly the same as yours.
Explain to your child that when talking with a classmate, your youngster could follow the pattern you have demonstrated.
For instance, a classmate could be asked to read the box on page 21 of the Origin of Life brochure.
Your child could then ask, “Is it true that the capacity of DNA for storing information still has no parallel in today’s computer age? ”
Instead of letting that comment stop the conversation, we could respectfully ask how long he has been an atheist and what caused him to adopt that view. After listening to his answers and complimenting him on giving the matter serious thought, we could ask if he felt that it would be wrong to read material that presented evidence that life was created.
If the householder is open - minded, he would likely say that it would be unreasonable to refuse to look at such evidence. We could then offer him either the brochure Was Life Created?
Why should we not settle for having a Bible student read answers from a Bible study aid?
Scenario 3: When conducting a Bible study, we might simply have the student repeat answers printed in a Bible study aid.
If we do so, however, we could stunt the spiritual growth of the student.
Because a student who repeats answers without meditating on them is unlikely to grow deep spiritual roots.
To help avoid that outcome, we need to ask our student how he feels about what he is learning. Try to discover if he agrees with the points made.
Then help him to reason on the Scriptures so that he will eventually be able to arrive at correct conclusions by himself.
When accompanying someone in the ministry, how can we work as a team? Jesus sent his disciples out in the preaching work by twos.
In your Bible, look up the scriptures that your partner is using.
Keep your attention turned to your partner and to the householder when either of them is talking.
Follow the discussion closely in case there is a need for you to assist your partner to overcome an objection.
What do we do well to remember, and why?
How can you and your partner assist each other while walking from door to door?
How does Daniel 2: 41 - 45 underscore the need for being zealous in the ministry?
Explain how godly conduct attracts people to true worship and to Jehovah God.
What singular honor do Jehovah’s Witnesses have, and how do you feel about it? MANY consider it a great honor to be given an award for a notable achievement.
But how much greater an honor it is to be sent by God as an ambassador or envoy to help people establish peaceful relations with their Creator!
Under the command of God and Christ, we beg people to “become reconciled to God. ”
We are being used by Jehovah to draw people to him. This is how millions in over 235 lands have been helped to enjoy good relations with God and thus have the hope of gaining everlasting life.
With heartfelt zeal, we invite “anyone that wishes take life’s water free. ”
Because we cherish this precious assignment and carry it out diligently, we may rightly be called a people “zealous for fine works. ”
Let us now consider how our zeal for fine works helps us to draw people to Jehovah.
Of what does “the very zeal of Jehovah ” assure us?
Referring to what the rulership of God’s Son will accomplish, Isaiah 9: 7 says: “The very zeal of Jehovah of armies will do this. ”
He set a perfect example of zealous perseverance in the ministry.
As the time for his sacrificial death drew near, Jesus ’ determination to help others come to know Jehovah intensified.
Upon being told to cut the tree down, the vinedresser requested time to fertilize it.
We are the only people on earth who offer hope of real solutions to mankind’s problems.
A newspaper columnist recently described as unanswerable the question, “Why do bad things happen to good people? ”
It is our Christian duty and privilege to share the Bible’s answers to such questions with all those willing to listen.
We have every reason to be “aglow with the spirit ” as we carry out our divine commission. With God’s blessing, our zealous evangelizing can help others come to know and love Jehovah.
We also have our older ones and those in poor health who do their best to attend Christian meetings and participate in the field service.
Such efforts affect how others view our ministry. In a letter to the Lincolnshire Boston Target, United Kingdom, a non - Witness reader said: “People are losing their faith in religions...
What do these church ministers do all day?
Your very presence in the ministry gives a powerful witness to observers
What can stimulate us to remain zealous for fine works in our ministry? What can we do, however, if we seem to be losing our zeal for the ministry?
Your honesty and hard work do not go unnoticed Why can it be said that our fine conduct draws people to Jehovah?
The second element of zealous works that attracts people to God is fine Christian conduct.
Why should we prayerfully consider the effects of our conduct?
Writing to the Corinthians, Paul pointed out that he had suffered tribulations, difficulties, beatings, and imprisonment.
To illustrate: Some years ago, there was an attempt to eliminate Jehovah’s Witnesses in an area of Angola. Two baptized Witnesses and 30 interested individuals who were attending our meetings were rounded up.
The intention was to intimidate people so that nobody would listen to Jehovah’s Witnesses. But after the public whipping, many members of the community approached the Witnesses and requested home Bible studies!
This example illustrates the far - reaching effect that our firm stand for Bible principles can have on others. We may wonder how many were reconciled to God because of the courageous stand taken by Peter and the other apostles.
In South Korea, about 700 Witnesses are in prison for their faith. This situation has gone on there for 60 years.
We also play a part in drawing people to Jehovah when we display such qualities as long - suffering, love, and kindness.
Some religious leaders have become wealthy by defrauding their flocks, using much of the money thus obtained to acquire expensive homes and automobiles — and in one case, an air - conditioned dog kennel.
Why are you determined to persevere in fine works?
How does displaying insight improve communication in marriage? Why do marriage mates need to show respect for each other?
What effect can cultivating humility have on a marriage?
How has good communication helped marriages? “ I WOULD rather spend time with my wife than with anyone else, ” said a brother in Canada.
A husband in Australia wrote: “In our 11 years together, not one day has passed when I have not spoken with my wife.
What factors can work against good communication?
Do you and your spouse enjoy pleasant communication, or do you find meaningful conversation to be a challenge?
Understandably, difficult situations may arise, for marriage unites two imperfect people who have different personalities, including traits that reflect their culture and upbringing. Moreover, a couple may have different communication styles.
What has helped couples to strengthen their marriage?
A successful marriage is, indeed, the product of hard work. But the results include immeasurable happiness.
Mates who love each other can truly enjoy their life together. Consider the loving marriage of Isaac and Rebekah.
Even after they had spent some time together as husband and wife, there is no indication that their affection for each other had waned. The same can be said of many couples today.
They have learned to convey their thoughts and feelings to each other honestly, yet kindly, by cultivating and displaying insight, love, deep respect, and humility. As we shall now see, when these fundamental qualities characterize a marriage, the lines of communication are always open.
How can insight help a married couple to understand each other more fully?
They appreciate warm, intimate communication, for it reassures them that they are loved. On the other hand, many men are less inclined to discuss their feelings and are more likely to talk about activities, problems, and solutions.
In making their marriage a success, what added motivation do Christian couples have?
In what practical ways can a couple strengthen their bond of love?
Love, “a perfect bond of union, ” is the most important quality in a marriage.
They become even closer friends and cherish each other’s company. Such marriages are nourished, not by just a few great deeds, as portrayed in the media, but by countless smaller acts — a hug, a kind remark, a thoughtful gesture, a telling smile, or a sincere “how was your day? ”
These little things can make a big difference in a marriage.
One couple who have been happily married for 19 years phone or text each other during the day “just to see how things are going, ” the husband said.
How often do I think about my spouse, perhaps reflecting on the qualities that attracted me to him or her in the first place? ’
Yet, their differences did not drive a wedge between them. Why not?
She, on the other hand, obeyed Abraham and thought of him as her “lord. ” When a couple lack respect for each other, this usually becomes evident in their pattern of speech or tone of voice.
Being “humble in mind ” plays a key role in keeping that stream flowing.
When my wife and I approach Jehovah together, we are reminded of our imperfection and God’s undeserved kindness.
Rather than courageously acknowledging a weakness, he points to faults in the other person. When hurt, instead of pursuing peace, he takes offense, perhaps retaliating with harsh words or icy silence.
Paul told fellow Christians: “Let the sun not set with you in a provoked state, neither allow place for the Devil. ”
How much better it is to discuss matters right away with reconciliation as the goal!
This includes having a humble spirit, which will help you to focus on the problem, not on yourself, lest you aggravate the situation. — Read Colossians 3: 12, 13.
How can humility help a couple to see their individual strengths in the right light? Humility and modesty help a married person focus on the strengths of his or her mate.
If her husband is humble and modest, he will not feel challenged by her but will encourage her to use her gifts, thus showing that he values and cherishes her. At the same time, a humble and modest wife will not flaunt her abilities or belittle her husband.
What can help present - day marriages to be happy and a cause for praise to God?
If you do these things, your marriage will bring joy to you and to your heavenly Father. Indeed, your feelings may well reflect those of a husband of 27 years, who wrote: “I cannot imagine life without my wife.
