How might children apply James 1: 19?
How do parents and children generally feel about one another, but what difficulty do they sometimes face?
Rather than focusing on any existing problems and differences that might have been troubling them, some 95 percent said that they would tell their parents: “I’m sorry ” and“ I love you so much. ” — For Parents Only, by Shaunti Feldhahn and Lisa Rice.
Although parents and children yearn to be close to one another, communication is sometimes difficult. Even when conversation may otherwise be frank and open, why are some topics avoided entirely?
What are some barriers to good communication?
Moses instructed Israelite fathers: “You must inculcate in your son and speak of them when you sit in your house and when you walk on the road and when you lie down and when you get up. ” Children spent the day either with their mother at home or with their father in the fields or at his workplace.
Why is communication a problem in many families today? How different life is today!
How do some parents ‘ buy out ’ more time to spend with their children? Can you ‘ buy out ’ time from other things so as to spend more of it with your family?
Some families agree to limit television viewing or computer use. Others strive to have at least one meal together each day.
Why should children listen to their parents? Children, do you obey your parents?
Tell your parents how you feel about things. This will help them to understand you.
They may tell you what you want to hear, but their advice may not help you at all. In fact, it could even harm you.
Lacking the wisdom and experience of older ones, most young people do not have a long - term view of things and may not be able to discern the consequences of certain actions. Remember the example of King Solomon’s son Rehoboam.
When he became the king of Israel, it would have been wise for him to follow the counsel of the older men. Instead, he followed the foolish advice of the younger men he had grown up with.
How might parents ’ reactions obstruct communication with their children? A barrier to communication also arises when parents react emotionally and negatively to what their children tell them.
Behind the “wild talk ” may be a heart in turmoil. As loving parents, use your ears to gain understanding and your tongue to heal.
