The birth of Ilaria brought on huge changes in our lives. Honestly, we had moments of discouragement, even as Proverbs 24: 10 mentioned: “Have you shown yourself discouraged in the day of distress?
As you can imagine, it took consistency — and sometimes firmness — to help Ilaria stay on the Christian path. I recall one occasion when she was playing with a friend but behaved badly.
Ilaria readily says that she appreciates the love for the ministry that her parents displayed. Now that she is married, she understands even more fully how important it is to obey Jehovah and follow his guidance.
How can we deepen our appreciation for Jehovah’s qualities?
What makes someone approachable?
How can we imitate Jehovah’s impartiality?
In fact, a list could be made of more than 40 different qualities of Jehovah, each of which has been discussed in our publications.
In what ways can we benefit from such a study? It can deepen our appreciation for our heavenly Father.
In turn, the deeper our appreciation for Jehovah, the stronger our desire to draw close to him and to imitate him. — Josh.
Appreciation may deepen gradually.
Similarly, we deepen our appreciation for a quality of Jehovah by getting acquainted with it, reflecting on it, and then imitating it in our own life.
In the case of each, we will consider: What is its meaning?
You can often discern whether a person is approachable or not by listening to what he says and by observing his body language — gestures, facial expressions, and other nonverbal signs.
How does Jehovah demonstrate that he is approachable?
We can speak to God at length at any time or place. We can approach him freely, knowing that he will never reproach us for doing so.
The prophet Isaiah likened Jehovah to a shepherd, saying: “With his arm he will collect together the lambs; and in his bosom he will carry them. ”
Jehovah wants us to be as close to him as a little lamb nestled in the bosom of a caring shepherd. What an approachable Father we have!
How can we imitate Jehovah in this regard?
Granted, each Christian needs to develop that quality to the full, but it is especially important for elders to be approachable.
Commenting on a reason why she felt that this quality is so important, one sister noted: “Only if an elder is approachable will we be able to benefit from any other fine qualities he may have. ”
But what makes a person approachable? What is a key to being approachable?
If an elder cares about others and is willing to give of himself in their behalf, his brothers and sisters, including young ones, will likely sense this attitude.
Why does wearing a convention badge often trigger a conversation, and what lesson can we learn from that?
Not long ago, a brother wore his convention badge when traveling home by airplane after attending a convention abroad.
Now, why does a convention badge often trigger a conversation?
Similarly, Christian elders want to give visible signs that tell their fellow believers: “Feel free to approach me. ” What are some of those signs?
Note the example Jesus set. Matthew reports that at a meeting with his disciples, “Jesus approached and spoke to them. ”
Likewise, elders today take the initiative to approach their fellow believers and speak to them. How can that affect the congregation?
An 88 - year - old pioneer sister observed: “The warm smiles and encouraging comments I receive from the elders when I enter the Kingdom Hall endear them to me. ” Another faithful sister added: “It may be viewed as a little thing, but when an elder welcomes me to the meeting with a smile, it means a lot to me. ”
A sister who has been serving Jehovah for nearly 50 years commented: “Elders who take some time to talk to me after the meeting make me feel valued. ”
Impartiality is another of Jehovah’s endearing qualities.
What does it mean to be impartial?
It involves being fair, free from having or showing bias or favoritism.
Because only if someone is impartial in his outlook will he be moved to treat all with impartiality. In the Christian Greek Scriptures, the expression “not partial ” literally means not a“ taker of faces, ” that is, not favoring one face over another.
Hence, one who is impartial will pay due regard, not to an individual’s outward appearance or circumstances, but to his or her character as a person.
What was it? They knew that their family, like other Israelite families, would receive a piece of land that had been allotted to their father.
However, their father, Zelophehad of the tribe of Manasseh, had died. According to custom, the right to take possession of the land would be passed to Zelophehad’s sons, but he had only daughters.
With no son in the family to receive the land, would the family’s land be handed to relatives and the daughters be left without a family inheritance?
The five sisters approached Moses and asked him: “Why should the name of our father be taken away from the midst of his family because he had no son? ”
They pleaded: “O give us a possession in the midst of our father’s brothers. ” Did Moses react by saying, ‘ There are no exceptions to the rule ’?
No, he “presented their case before Jehovah. ”
From then on, all Israelite women who faced the same plight would be protected.
What a kind and impartial decision that was!
Jehovah treated these women, who were in a vulnerable position, with dignity, as he did Israelites who had more favorable circumstances.
This is just one of many Bible accounts that illustrate this heartwarming truth: Jehovah treats all of his servants with impartiality. — 1 Sam.
Remember, impartiality has two aspects.
Only if we are impartial will we treat others without partiality.
True, all of us like to think of ourselves as being open - minded and impartial. You will likely agree, though, that it is not always easy to evaluate our own feelings objectively.
So, what could we do to find out if we are known as being unbiased? Well, when Jesus was interested in knowing what people were saying about him, he asked his trusted friends: “Who are men saying the Son of man is? ”
You could ask some friend whom you can count on for candor whether you have a reputation for being impartial. If he or she concedes that there seem to be some lingering traces of racial, social, or economic partiality, what should you do?
Pray earnestly to Jehovah about your feelings, begging him to help you adjust your attitude so that it will reflect his impartiality to a fuller degree. — Matt.
Indeed, as we take time to reflect on how approachable and impartial Jehovah is, our appreciation for him deepens.
Deepened appreciation, in turn, ought to move us to imitate Jehovah’s qualities to the full, demonstrating them in our dealings with fellow believers and with those to whom we preach.
What are two of Jehovah’s qualities for which we can deepen our appreciation?
How can we imitate Jehovah’s generosity?
In what ways can we imitate Jehovah’s reasonableness?
Jehovah’s friends have what opportunity?
No doubt, the same is true in countless marriages and friendships. We enjoy getting better acquainted with those whom we love.
What will we consider in this article?
What is the essence of true generosity?
What does it mean to be generous?
In what ways does Jehovah demonstrate generosity?
Indeed, “Jehovah is good to all. ” He “makes his sun rise upon wicked people and good and makes it rain upon righteous people and unrighteous. ”
That is why the apostle Paul, when speaking to unbelievers, could say that Jehovah “did good, giving you rains from heaven and fruitful seasons, filling your hearts to the full with food and good cheer. ”
To my surprise, several customers came to the restaurant that night.
What is Jehovah’s most generous gift?
Jehovah’s most generous gift is available to everyone. What is it?
The ransom sacrifice of his Son. Jesus said: “God loved the world so much that he gave his only - begotten Son, in order that everyone exercising faith in him might not be destroyed but have everlasting life. ”
The Israelites were encouraged to imitate Jehovah’s generosity (See paragraph 9)
How can we imitate Jehovah’s generosity?
We gladly use our resources to give gifts to our loved ones and to help those in need.
Some Christians take this practical approach: Whenever they receive a gift, they look for an opportunity to give someone else a gift.
What is one outstanding way to be generous?
One of the best ways to be generous is to give of ourselves in word and deed.
How can we do that? By using our time and energy to help and encourage others.
To test how we are doing in this regard, we might ask ourselves: ‘ Do others sense that I’m willing to give of myself and listen to their concerns?
If someone asks for assistance with a project or an errand, do I say yes whenever possible?
When was the last time that I gave sincere commendation to a family member or a fellow believer? ’
Those “valuable things ” include our time, energy, and resources, which we can freely spend in his service.
What does it mean to be reasonable?
Another one of Jehovah’s endearing qualities is reasonableness.
Rather, he strives to be gentle in his dealings with others, taking into consideration their circumstances. He is willing to listen to others and, when appropriate, to yield to their wishes and adjust his requirements.
How did the Mosaic Law reflect Jehovah’s reasonableness?
Consider another example of Jehovah’s reasonableness as manifested in the Mosaic Law. If an Israelite was too poor to offer a lamb or a goat as a sacrifice, he could offer instead two turtledoves or two pigeons.
In that case, Jehovah allowed the needy Israelite to offer a little flour. However, note this important detail: It had to be, not just any flour, but “fine flour, ” the kind used for honored guests.
As you arrive at the tabernacle with a little flour to offer as a sacrifice, you notice wealthier Israelites bringing livestock. You might feel embarrassed about your seemingly insignificant sacrifice of flour.
In effect, Jehovah was saying to poorer Israelites: ‘ I realize that you cannot offer as much as others can, but I also know that what you are giving me is your best. ’ Truly, Jehovah displays reasonableness by taking into account his servants ’ limitations and their circumstances. — Ps.
You can be sure that Jehovah accepts what sort of service?
We can draw comfort from knowing that in his reasonableness, Jehovah accepts our whole - souled service.
How can we imitate Jehovah’s reasonableness? Think again of the way that Jehovah dealt with Lot.
Can you listen to your children’s requests and, where appropriate, accede to their wishes?
How can elders strive to imitate Jehovah’s reasonableness?
Likewise, some brothers and sisters are very limited in what they can do in the ministry, perhaps because of health problems or advanced age. What if these dear ones feel disheartened because of their limitations?
On the one hand, we exert ourselves, not holding back in our service. On the other hand, we remember that Jehovah never asks more of us than we can give.
In what ways can we imitate Jehovah’s loyalty?
How can we imitate Jehovah’s forgiveness?
Why do you want to continue to deepen your appreciation for Jehovah’s qualities?
All of us appreciate friends who are loyal and forgiving.
It is as the psalmist put it: “You, O Jehovah, are good and ready to forgive; and the loving - kindness to all those calling upon you is abundant. ”
What does it mean to be loyal and forgiving?
How does Jehovah display those beautiful qualities?
And how can we imitate his example?
A loyal person is not fickle.
Rather, he lovingly attaches himself to someone (or something), sticking closely to that person (or thing) even through difficult circumstances.
One such worshipper, King David, testified to Jehovah’s loyalty.
Jehovah cherishes the loyalty of his worshippers, and he repays it with loyalty toward them. — Prov.
It reminds me that no matter what the circumstance might be, no matter how bleak the situation might seem, Jehovah will be there for me as long as I remain loyal to him. ” No doubt, you feel the same way. — Rom.
In what other ways does Jehovah demonstrate loyalty, and with what benefit to his worshippers?
In what other ways does Jehovah demonstrate loyalty?
He remains true to his standards.
He always makes decisions based on his unchanging standards of right and wrong.
In addition, Jehovah demonstrates loyalty by remaining faithful to his word of promise. Jehovah’s loyalty thus benefits all of his faithful worshippers.
How so? When we do our best to adhere to Jehovah’s standards, we can be confident that he will keep his promise to bless us. — Isa.
What is one way that we can imitate God’s loyalty?
How can we imitate Jehovah’s loyalty?
One way is by taking action in behalf of those who are facing difficult circumstances.
For example, do you know of a fellow believer who is discouraged, perhaps because of health problems, family opposition, or personal failings?
Why not take the initiative to offer that person some “good words, comforting words ”?
So we do not take even the first step down a path that could lead to adultery. In addition, we show loyalty to our fellow believers by shunning hurtful gossip or slander, refusing to spread such negative talk or even to listen to it. — Prov.
How do we do that? By striving to view things the way that he views them — loving what he loves and hating what he hates — and then conducting ourselves accordingly.
Still, she puts forth determined effort to maintain her integrity to Jehovah. Do we not appreciate such sterling examples of loyalty?
What does it mean to be forgiving?
When a sinner genuinely repents, he deeply regrets his wrong course. He is also determined not to repeat his sin.
Moreover, true repentance moves a sinner to “turn around, ” abandoning his wrong course and pursuing a course that is pleasing to God. If Peter’s listeners would manifest such genuine repentance, what would be the result?
That expression comes from a Greek word that means to “wipe out, erase. ” So when Jehovah forgives, he wipes the slate clean.
Jehovah says: “I shall forgive their error, and their sin I shall remember no more. ”
So Jehovah assures us that once he forgives, he will never in the future act against us because of those sins.
How can we gain comfort from meditating on Jehovah’s forgiveness?
Significantly, though, in order to be forgiven by God, we must imitate Jehovah’s forgiveness in our dealings with others.
May our prayers for forgiveness be from the heart (See paragraph 17) What can help us if we have been hurt by a fellow believer?
Of course, it is not always easy to forgive. Even some anointed Christians in the first century apparently found it challenging to settle their differences.
If we have been hurt by a fellow believer, what can help us?
The lesson for us? A sincere prayer in behalf of someone who has offended us may help us to let go of resentment.
We can do that by becoming acquainted with his qualities, reflecting on them, and then imitating them in our own life.
As we do so, we will undoubtedly come to agree more and more with the psalmist who sang: “As for me, the drawing near to God is good for me. ” — Ps.
