In the verses that lead up to Matthew 24: 46, the word “coming ” refers consistently to the time when Jesus comes to pronounce and execute judgment during the great tribulation. Also, as we considered in paragraph 12, Jesus ’ ‘ arriving ’ mentioned at Matthew 25: 31 refers to that same future time of judgment.
We first considered that the great tribulation did not begin in 1914 but will start when the United Nations attacks Babylon the Great.
