If no one answers, we could be tempted to look through the window or walk around the property, searching for the householder.
Nevertheless, we wisely avoid doing anything that could unduly disturb people in our witnessing territory. The apostle Paul wrote: “In no way are we giving any cause for stumbling, so that no fault may be found with our ministry. ”
In our territory, when are people usually at home?
When are they likely to be receptive?
