First, “Jehovah knows those who belong to him ” and second,“ Let everyone calling on the name of Jehovah renounce unrighteousness. ”
How is this lesson relevant to the issue of apostasy within the congregation? How did the actions of apostates affect faithful ones in Paul’s day?
As one “calling on the name of Jehovah, ” Timothy was also reminded of his own responsibility to reject the unrighteous influence of counterfeit Christians.
What confidence can we have?
We can likewise derive spiritual strength from Paul’s inspired words.
What type of worship does Jehovah not tolerate?
