The Boy Scouts are a worldwide organization founded in 1908 in Great Britain by a lieutenant general of the British army, Robert Stephenson Smyth Baden - Powell. In 1916 he founded the Wolf Cubs (or Cub Scouts) for younger boys in my age group.
I liked our weekend campouts in the country — sleeping in tents, wearing uniforms, and marching to the sound of drums. I particularly enjoyed the time with the other Scouts, including our singing around a campfire in the evening and playing games in the forest.
