Read or sing to the patient, choosing literature and songs that are upbuilding and enjoyable to him. Many people are comforted when a family member holds their hand and speaks softly to them.
Hearing may still remain very acute although the may seem asleep so do not say anything in their presence you would not say to them when awake. ” If possible, pray together.
The Bible relates that on one occasion, the apostle Paul and his companions were under extreme pressure and were very uncertain even of their lives. What assistance did they seek?
Swabbing glycerin on the mouth and lips and placing a moist washcloth on the forehead may keep the patient comfortable.
Desire to be alone or with very few people. Keep the environment quiet and calm.
Restlessness.
